WEBVTT

00:02.509 --> 00:03.760
KATARA: Water.

00:04.719 --> 00:05.929
Earth.

00:06.679 --> 00:07.889
Fire.

00:09.015 --> 00:10.225
Air.

00:11.309 --> 00:14.771
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:15.313 --> 00:18.816
Then, everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.692 --> 00:22.570
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

00:22.654 --> 00:23.738
could stop them.

00:23.821 --> 00:26.741
But when the world needed him most,
he vanished.

00:27.116 --> 00:28.368
100 years passed,

00:28.451 --> 00:30.995
and my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar,

00:31.079 --> 00:32.580
an airbender named Aang.

00:33.039 --> 00:35.083
And although
his airbending skills are great

00:35.166 --> 00:37.794
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone.

00:37.877 --> 00:39.087
AANG: Oof.

00:39.170 --> 00:41.965
But I believe Aang can save the world.

00:42.298 --> 00:43.967
[ ♪... ]

00:47.971 --> 00:50.473
( MAN READING )

00:50.765 --> 00:51.933
I need you, Zuko.

00:52.016 --> 00:56.771
I've plotted every move of this day,
and the only way we win is together.

00:59.607 --> 01:01.276
We've done it, Zuko.

01:01.359 --> 01:04.070
The Fire Nation has conquered Ba Sing Se.

01:04.153 --> 01:05.446
ZUKO: I betrayed uncle.

01:05.780 --> 01:07.657
AZULA: No, he betrayed you.

01:08.575 --> 01:12.620
When you return home,
father will welcome you as a war hero.

01:12.704 --> 01:14.163
But I don't have the Avatar.

01:14.581 --> 01:16.541
What if father doesn't restore my honor?

01:19.502 --> 01:20.878
[ ♪... ]

01:28.052 --> 01:29.637
( GROANING )

01:35.518 --> 01:36.811
( GRUNTING )

01:41.316 --> 01:42.942
What happened?

01:49.032 --> 01:50.241
Oh, no!

01:57.540 --> 01:59.208
( GRUNTING )

02:01.085 --> 02:02.795
MAN: You hear something?

02:02.879 --> 02:04.422
( GASPING )

02:06.883 --> 02:07.884
MAN: He's awake.

02:08.551 --> 02:09.636
( PANTING )

02:09.719 --> 02:11.262
Stop, wait!

02:12.347 --> 02:14.223
( GRUNTING )

02:18.311 --> 02:19.312
Momo?

02:20.063 --> 02:21.356
( SQUEAKING )

02:24.025 --> 02:26.569
Twinkle-toes, that's got to be you.

02:27.862 --> 02:29.364
Aang, you're awake.

02:29.447 --> 02:30.573
AANG: Are you sure?

02:31.032 --> 02:32.867
I feel like I'm dreaming.

02:32.950 --> 02:33.951
You're not dreaming.

02:34.243 --> 02:35.620
You're finally awake.

02:35.703 --> 02:38.289
Aang, good to see you
back with the living, buddy.

02:39.123 --> 02:40.166
Sokka?

02:40.917 --> 02:42.502
-( SIGHING )
- TOPH: Uh-oh, somebody catch him.

02:42.585 --> 02:43.795
He's gonna...

02:45.296 --> 02:47.590
( GROWLING )

02:56.349 --> 02:57.642
Aren't you cold?

02:58.893 --> 03:00.728
I've got a lot on my mind.

03:01.312 --> 03:03.231
It's been so long.

03:03.314 --> 03:05.441
Over three years since I was home.

03:06.609 --> 03:08.778
I wonder what's changed.

03:08.861 --> 03:10.571
I wonder how I've changed.

03:10.655 --> 03:12.824
( YAWNING ) I just asked if you were cold.

03:12.907 --> 03:15.201
I didn't ask for your whole life story.

03:17.662 --> 03:19.288
Stop worrying.

03:30.049 --> 03:32.176
AANG: Why are we on a Fire Nation ship?

03:32.260 --> 03:34.262
Why is everyone dressed this way?

03:34.345 --> 03:37.306
And why am I the only one
who's completely out of it?

03:37.390 --> 03:38.975
You need to take it easy, ok?

03:39.058 --> 03:41.018
You got hurt pretty bad.

03:42.937 --> 03:44.439
I like your hair.

03:44.522 --> 03:45.898
I have hair?

03:46.774 --> 03:48.151
How long was I out?

03:48.234 --> 03:49.569
A few weeks.

03:49.652 --> 03:50.862
Everything ok?

03:50.945 --> 03:52.113
We're fine, dad.

03:52.447 --> 03:55.408
I'm Hakoda, Katara and Sokka's father.

03:55.491 --> 03:58.077
He knows who you are.
I just called you "dad," didn't I?

03:58.828 --> 04:00.079
I guess you're right.

04:01.539 --> 04:04.000
Nice to officially meet you, Chief Hakoda.

04:04.083 --> 04:05.460
It's an honor to meet you.

04:05.793 --> 04:07.837
Great, great.
Now you guys have finally met,

04:07.920 --> 04:09.881
so would you mind
giving us a little privacy?

04:10.757 --> 04:12.008
Of course.

04:14.343 --> 04:16.387
Are you mad at your dad or something?

04:17.096 --> 04:19.474
What? Not at all. Why would you say that?

04:19.974 --> 04:21.392
( SHRUGS, GROANS )

04:22.477 --> 04:23.770
Maybe we should go upstairs.

04:24.270 --> 04:25.897
You need a healing session.

04:31.277 --> 04:33.529
Tell me where your pain
feels most intense.

04:33.613 --> 04:35.406
( GRUNTING ) A little higher.

04:35.490 --> 04:36.491
( GRUNTS )

04:43.998 --> 04:45.124
Wow.

04:45.208 --> 04:47.460
You're definitely in the right area there.

04:47.835 --> 04:50.630
I can feel a lot of energy
twisted up around there.

04:50.922 --> 04:52.548
Let me just see if I can...

05:02.308 --> 05:03.643
I went down.

05:03.726 --> 05:05.436
I didn't just get hurt, did I?

05:05.520 --> 05:07.146
It was worse than that.

05:07.230 --> 05:10.191
I was gone, but you brought me back.

05:10.733 --> 05:13.486
I just used the spirit water
from the North Pole.

05:13.569 --> 05:14.821
I don't know what I did, exactly.

05:15.863 --> 05:17.281
You saved me.

05:17.782 --> 05:19.200
You need to rest.

05:22.203 --> 05:26.958
WOMAN 1: Your Princess Azula,
clever and beautiful,

05:27.041 --> 05:32.672
disguised herself as the enemy
and entered the Earth Kingdom's capital.

05:32.755 --> 05:37.510
WOMAN 2: In Ba Sing Se,
she found her brother Zuko,

05:37.593 --> 05:40.471
and together, they faced the Avatar.

05:40.555 --> 05:46.310
BOTH WOMEN: And the Avatar fell,
and the Earth Kingdom fell.

05:46.394 --> 05:50.898
WOMAN 1: Azula's agents
quickly overtook the entire city.

05:51.274 --> 05:54.610
They went to Ba Sing Se's great walls...

05:54.694 --> 05:57.530
BOTH WOMEN: ...and brought them down.

06:05.496 --> 06:09.500
WOMAN 2: The armies of the Fire Nation
surged through the wall

06:09.584 --> 06:15.381
and swarmed over Ba Sing Se,
securing our victory.

06:16.132 --> 06:17.758
( BABY CRYING )

06:27.018 --> 06:30.354
BOTH WOMEN: Now the heroes
have returned home.

06:30.438 --> 06:34.066
WOMAN 1: Your princess, Azula.

06:34.150 --> 06:37.320
( CHEERING AND APPLAUSE )

06:37.737 --> 06:42.700
And after three long years,
your prince has returned.

06:43.159 --> 06:44.493
Zuko.

06:45.745 --> 06:51.250
( CHEERING AND APPLAUSE )

06:53.502 --> 06:56.547
After what happened in Ba Sing Se,
we had to get you to safety.

06:57.590 --> 06:59.133
We flew back to Chameleon Bay,

06:59.216 --> 07:01.677
where we found my father
and the other water tribe men.

07:03.387 --> 07:06.349
The Earth King decided he wanted
to travel the world in disguise,

07:06.432 --> 07:07.767
so he set off alone.

07:07.850 --> 07:09.435
Well, not completely alone.

07:09.518 --> 07:10.686
( GROWLING )

07:13.814 --> 07:16.275
Soon, the bay was overrun
with Fire Nation ships.

07:16.359 --> 07:19.946
Rather than fight them all, we captured
a single ship and made it our disguise.

07:20.321 --> 07:22.323
Since then, we've been traveling west.

07:22.406 --> 07:24.492
We crossed through the Serpent's Pass
a few days ago.

07:25.034 --> 07:27.578
We've seen a few Fire Nation ships,
but none have bothered us.

07:28.663 --> 07:29.664
So, what now?

07:29.747 --> 07:32.792
We've been working on
a modified version of the invasion plan.

07:33.042 --> 07:35.419
It's Sokka's invasion plan.

07:36.128 --> 07:37.922
Yes, Sokka's plan.

07:38.673 --> 07:42.051
We won't be able to mount a massive
invasion without the Earth King's armies

07:42.134 --> 07:45.721
But the solar eclipse will still
leave the Fire Nation vulnerable.

07:46.138 --> 07:47.848
So we're planning a smaller invasion.

07:47.932 --> 07:51.018
Just a ragtag team of our friends
and allies from around the Earth Kingdom.

07:51.102 --> 07:53.187
We already ran into
Pipsqueak and The Duke.

07:53.813 --> 07:55.481
Good to see you again, Aang.

07:56.023 --> 07:59.568
And the best part is, the eclipse
isn't even our biggest advantage.

07:59.652 --> 08:01.904
We have a secret.

08:02.488 --> 08:04.240
- You.
- Me?

08:04.323 --> 08:06.617
Yep, the whole world thinks you're dead.

08:07.076 --> 08:08.703
Isn't that great?

08:13.374 --> 08:14.375
[ ♪... ]

08:14.917 --> 08:16.252
The world thinks I'm dead?

08:16.794 --> 08:18.212
How is that good news?

08:18.295 --> 08:19.296
That's terrible.

08:19.672 --> 08:20.715
No, it's great.

08:20.798 --> 08:23.009
It means the Fire Nation
won't be hunting us anymore.

08:23.217 --> 08:26.095
And even better, they won't be
expecting you on the day of black sun.

08:26.178 --> 08:27.722
No, no, no, no, no.

08:28.139 --> 08:29.682
You have no idea.

08:29.765 --> 08:31.225
This is so messed up.

08:31.475 --> 08:33.978
( HORN BLARING )

08:34.311 --> 08:35.938
I'll handle this.

08:36.022 --> 08:37.356
The Avatar is back.

08:37.440 --> 08:38.691
( GRUNTING )

08:39.191 --> 08:40.359
KATARA: Aang, wait.

08:40.443 --> 08:42.903
Remember, they don't know
we're not Fire Nation.

08:46.407 --> 08:48.534
Everyone, just stay calm.

08:48.617 --> 08:50.453
Bato and I will take care of this.

08:56.125 --> 08:58.669
I hate not being able to do anything.

08:58.753 --> 09:00.504
Hopefully, you won't need to.

09:13.059 --> 09:15.144
Commander, why are you off course?

09:15.519 --> 09:17.855
All western fleet ships
are supposed to be moving

09:17.938 --> 09:20.316
toward Ba Sing Se
to support the occupation.

09:20.733 --> 09:23.402
Actually, we're from the eastern fleet.

09:23.486 --> 09:25.154
We have orders to deliver some cargo.

09:25.488 --> 09:27.907
Ah, eastern fleet.

09:27.990 --> 09:31.911
Well, nice of Admiral Chan to let us know
he was sending one of his ships our way.

09:32.328 --> 09:34.955
I'm sure Admiral Chan
meant no disrespect, sir.

09:35.039 --> 09:38.334
I mean, how hard is it to write a quick
note and send a hawk our way?

09:39.001 --> 09:42.379
Next time, we'll send two hawks,
to be sure you get the message.

09:44.632 --> 09:48.094
Sir, Admiral Chan has been on leave
for two months at Ember Island.

09:48.177 --> 09:51.472
What? Why doesn't anyone
ever tell me anything?

09:51.555 --> 09:52.765
Something's not right.

09:52.848 --> 09:54.016
They should've known that.

09:54.100 --> 09:55.476
I think this is a captured ship.

09:56.685 --> 09:58.938
Just stay quiet
until we're safely across the ramp.

09:59.396 --> 10:01.398
Then we'll sink this ship.

10:02.483 --> 10:03.526
They know!

10:06.112 --> 10:07.404
( GRUNTING )

10:08.572 --> 10:10.241
( SCREAMING )

10:14.829 --> 10:15.830
( GRUNTING )

10:36.475 --> 10:37.893
( QUACKING )

10:37.977 --> 10:39.395
You seem so downcast.

10:39.645 --> 10:41.522
Has Mai gotten to you already?

10:41.605 --> 10:44.775
Though actually, Mai has been
in a strangely good mood lately.

10:45.359 --> 10:46.944
I haven't seen dad yet.

10:47.027 --> 10:50.364
I haven't seen him in three years,
since I was banished.

10:50.447 --> 10:51.699
AZULA: So what?

10:51.782 --> 10:54.034
So, I didn't capture the Avatar.

10:54.535 --> 10:56.912
Who cares? The Avatar's dead.

10:58.998 --> 11:03.252
Unless you think he somehow
miraculously survived.

11:05.379 --> 11:08.007
KATARA: This is water from
the spirit oasis at the North Pole.

11:08.299 --> 11:12.261
It has special properties, so I've been
saving it for something important.

11:13.637 --> 11:14.972
No.

11:15.055 --> 11:17.016
There's no way he could've survived.

11:21.854 --> 11:25.232
Well, then I'm sure you have
nothing to worry about.

11:40.247 --> 11:41.790
Load the Toph!

11:41.874 --> 11:43.375
( GRUNTING )

12:21.872 --> 12:23.249
I'm gonna give us some cover.

12:45.271 --> 12:47.856
I can't just stand by and do nothing.

12:47.940 --> 12:49.066
Aang, no!

12:49.775 --> 12:52.528
You're still hurt,
and you have to stay secret.

12:52.611 --> 12:54.321
Just let us handle this.

12:55.030 --> 12:56.115
Fine.

13:07.459 --> 13:08.585
TOPH: How we doing?

13:08.669 --> 13:10.004
Things couldn't get much worse.

13:10.087 --> 13:12.298
( DRAGON GROWLING )

13:13.590 --> 13:16.844
The universe just loves
proving me wrong, doesn't it?

13:16.927 --> 13:18.304
You make it too easy.

13:31.859 --> 13:33.777
Thank you, the universe.

13:44.663 --> 13:45.956
Hey, Aang.

13:46.040 --> 13:47.750
We're going into town to find some dinner.

13:48.250 --> 13:49.460
( STOMACH GRUMBLING )

13:49.543 --> 13:51.587
Well, I am pretty hungry.

13:51.670 --> 13:53.172
Maybe dinner's a good idea.

13:53.964 --> 13:55.382
Here, tie this around your head.

13:55.466 --> 13:56.800
It'll cover your arrow.

13:57.259 --> 14:00.095
I'm not going out
if I can't wear my arrow proudly.

14:00.637 --> 14:01.638
Aang, come on.

14:01.722 --> 14:02.723
Be practical.

14:03.474 --> 14:04.850
You guys go ahead without us.

14:04.933 --> 14:06.226
We'll catch up with you.

14:08.771 --> 14:12.441
I think I understand why
being a secret bothers you so much.

14:12.524 --> 14:14.401
You don't want people to think you failed.

14:14.485 --> 14:15.778
You're right, I don't.

14:15.861 --> 14:18.155
But the problem is, I did fail.

14:18.572 --> 14:20.407
Aang, that's not true.

14:20.491 --> 14:21.992
It is true.

14:22.076 --> 14:23.535
I was in Ba Sing Se.

14:23.619 --> 14:26.622
I was there, but I lost.

14:27.206 --> 14:29.291
And now, the Earth Kingdom
has fallen for good.

14:30.000 --> 14:31.418
It's not for good.

14:31.502 --> 14:33.045
Remember, there's still a plan.

14:33.128 --> 14:34.296
The invasion.

14:34.380 --> 14:36.423
And I hate the invasion plan, too.

14:36.507 --> 14:40.511
I don't want you or anyone else
risking your lives to fix my mistakes.

14:41.261 --> 14:44.056
I've always known
that I would have to face the Fire Lord

14:44.139 --> 14:45.849
But now I know I need to do it alone.

14:46.642 --> 14:47.976
Aang.

14:48.060 --> 14:49.228
Katara, please.

14:49.770 --> 14:52.106
Just go, please.

14:54.191 --> 14:55.859
Is there anything you need?

14:57.653 --> 14:59.154
I need to redeem myself.

14:59.947 --> 15:01.907
I need my honor back.

15:12.751 --> 15:15.254
( SIGHING )

15:28.934 --> 15:30.269
I brought you some food.

15:33.188 --> 15:34.398
Oh, no.

15:50.414 --> 15:53.125
You have been away for a long time.

15:53.667 --> 15:56.462
I see the weight of your travels
has changed you.

15:57.004 --> 16:00.257
You have redeemed yourself, my son.

16:05.471 --> 16:07.181
Welcome home.

16:12.603 --> 16:13.979
[ ♪... ]

16:27.451 --> 16:29.411
I'll leave you two alone.

16:30.871 --> 16:32.206
What's wrong, Katara?

16:32.289 --> 16:33.457
He left.

16:33.540 --> 16:34.541
What?

16:34.625 --> 16:35.626
Aang.

16:35.709 --> 16:37.836
He just took his glider and disappeared.

16:37.920 --> 16:41.965
He has this ridiculous notion
that he has to save the world alone

16:42.049 --> 16:43.717
That it's all his responsibility.

16:44.259 --> 16:46.428
Maybe that's his way of being brave.

16:46.512 --> 16:49.306
It's not brave. It's selfish and stupid.

16:49.389 --> 16:52.184
We could be helping him,
and I know the world needs him,

16:52.267 --> 16:54.895
but doesn't he know how much
that we need him too?

16:54.978 --> 16:56.522
How could he just leave us behind?

16:58.398 --> 17:00.692
You're talking about me too, aren't you?

17:01.068 --> 17:03.487
How could you leave us, dad?

17:03.570 --> 17:07.032
I mean, I know we had Gran-Gran,
and she loved us, but...

17:07.115 --> 17:09.701
But we were just so lost without you.

17:10.160 --> 17:11.537
( SOBBING )

17:11.620 --> 17:13.247
I'm so sorry, Katara.

17:16.041 --> 17:18.168
I understand why you left.

17:18.252 --> 17:22.214
I really do,
and I know that you had to go,

17:22.297 --> 17:25.884
so why do I still feel this way?

17:25.968 --> 17:29.972
I was so sad and angry, and hurt.

17:30.305 --> 17:33.100
I love you more than anything.

17:33.183 --> 17:35.686
You and your brother are my entire world.

17:36.103 --> 17:40.816
I thought about you every day I was gone,
and every night when I went to sleep

17:40.899 --> 17:44.987
I would lie awake
missing you so much it would ache.

17:48.532 --> 17:51.118
OZAI: I am proud of you, Prince Zuko.

17:51.201 --> 17:55.205
I am proud because you
and your sister conquered Ba Sing Se.

17:55.581 --> 18:00.877
I am proud because when your loyalty
was tested by your treacherous uncle

18:00.961 --> 18:04.506
you did the right thing
and captured the traitor

18:04.840 --> 18:09.428
And I am proudest of all
of your most legendary accomplishment.

18:09.761 --> 18:12.347
You slayed the Avatar.

18:13.181 --> 18:14.349
What did you hear?

18:14.433 --> 18:16.059
Azula told me everything.

18:17.019 --> 18:19.021
She said she was amazed and impressed

18:19.104 --> 18:24.151
with your power and ferocity
at the moment of truth.

18:31.283 --> 18:32.784
AANG: Blockade.

18:35.245 --> 18:36.413
( INHALING )

18:46.381 --> 18:47.883
( GASPING )

18:57.225 --> 18:58.477
( GRUNTING )

19:15.786 --> 19:16.870
( GRUNTING )

19:21.708 --> 19:22.793
ZUKO: Why'd you do it?

19:24.336 --> 19:26.963
You're going to have to be
a little more specific.

19:27.506 --> 19:30.717
Why did you tell father
that I was the one who killed the Avatar?

19:30.801 --> 19:32.719
AZULA: Can't this wait until morning?

19:33.053 --> 19:34.304
It can't.

19:34.846 --> 19:36.473
( SIGHING ) Fine.

19:37.557 --> 19:40.060
You seemed so worried
about how father would treat you

19:40.143 --> 19:42.437
because you hadn't captured the Avatar.

19:42.521 --> 19:45.732
I figured, if I gave you the credit,
you'd have nothing to worry about.

19:45.816 --> 19:46.817
But why?

19:46.900 --> 19:49.194
Call it a generous gesture.

19:49.277 --> 19:53.281
I wanted to thank you for your help,
and I was happy to share the glory.

19:53.532 --> 19:54.783
You're lying.

19:55.575 --> 19:56.827
If you say so.

19:57.494 --> 19:59.287
You have another motive for doing this.

19:59.371 --> 20:01.373
I just haven't figured out what it is.

20:01.456 --> 20:02.708
Please, Zuko.

20:03.083 --> 20:05.293
What ulterior motive could I have?

20:05.377 --> 20:07.087
What could I possibly gain

20:07.170 --> 20:10.507
by letting you get all the glory
for defeating the Avatar?

20:10.757 --> 20:14.511
Unless, somehow,
the Avatar was actually alive.

20:15.345 --> 20:19.599
All that glory would suddenly
turn to shame and foolishness.

20:21.184 --> 20:24.980
But you said yourself,
that was impossible.

20:25.897 --> 20:27.524
Sleep well, Zu Zu.

20:38.869 --> 20:41.621
( SCREAMING )

20:48.253 --> 20:50.297
( GASPING )

20:53.133 --> 20:55.343
I'm not gonna make it.

20:55.427 --> 20:56.428
I failed.

20:56.511 --> 20:58.680
( THUNDER RUMBLING )

20:58.764 --> 21:00.056
Roku?

21:00.140 --> 21:02.225
You haven't failed, Aang.

21:02.934 --> 21:04.978
But everyone thinks I'm dead again.

21:05.520 --> 21:09.775
They think I've abandoned them,
and I'm losing this war.

21:09.858 --> 21:11.818
I'm letting the whole world down.

21:12.152 --> 21:16.907
ROKU: If anyone is to blame
for the state of the world, it is me.

21:16.990 --> 21:20.118
I should've seen this war coming,
and prevented it.

21:20.744 --> 21:25.207
You inherited my problems and my mistakes

21:25.290 --> 21:30.504
But I believe you are destined
to redeem me, and save the world.

21:30.879 --> 21:32.172
I don't know.

21:33.173 --> 21:35.300
YUE: You already saved the world.

21:38.428 --> 21:40.472
And you'll save the world again.

21:40.764 --> 21:42.891
But you can't give up.

21:47.687 --> 21:48.772
You're right.

21:49.189 --> 21:50.690
I won't give up.

22:29.312 --> 22:31.356
( CHIRPING )

22:34.025 --> 22:36.278
( GROANING )

22:40.448 --> 22:41.825
You're ok.

22:46.288 --> 22:48.665
( GROWLING )

22:51.251 --> 22:52.836
I have so much to do.

22:52.919 --> 22:54.963
I know, but you'll have our help.

22:55.046 --> 22:56.840
You didn't think
you could get out of training

22:56.923 --> 22:58.842
just by coming to the Fire Nation,
did you?

23:00.510 --> 23:02.053
What about the invasion?

23:02.137 --> 23:05.515
We'll join up with my dad and the invasion
force on the day of the eclipse.

23:05.599 --> 23:07.100
Hey, what's...

23:08.059 --> 23:10.812
Oh, it's your glider.

23:11.563 --> 23:12.856
That's ok.

23:14.691 --> 23:17.777
If someone saw it,
it would give away my identity.

23:18.236 --> 23:20.822
It's better for now
that no one knows I'm alive.

23:48.558 --> 23:50.018
[ ♪... ]
